# Everything in device/ is uploaded to the miner byte for byte by
# install_rxd.py and then run by busybox sh or Python 2.7. A CRLF line ending
# that survived a clone on Windows would reach the miner intact and break the
# script there - busybox treats the \r as part of the command. Force LF so a
# clone on any platform produces files the miner can actually run.
device/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# The web assets are served to a browser, which does not care, but keeping them
# LF means the firmware package builds byte-identically on every machine.
*.css text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Never let Git's text handling touch a firmware image or a certificate: a
# single altered byte makes an encrypted .bgz undecryptable.
*.bgz binary
*.tar binary
*.crt binary
*.key binary
*.png binary
